<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_TarBlaze.xml                       UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S1 build pass. The burning-wall Thing RM_CompFloodIgniter
  spawns into every ignited tar cell (spawned by code via
  FireUtility.TryStartFireIn today — see the C# note below on why that call
  is being repointed) and self-manages for its own burn duration.

  🔴 FIRE-AVOIDANCE / PATHING DECISION (resolves the spike pass's own named
  build-shape gap, SUMP_MECHANICS_1.md "spike pass" > "Engine ground-truth"
  #1 — see RM_CompTimedTerrainBurn.cs's header for the full citation trail):
  RUT_TarBlaze is NOT a Fire subclass. It is a plain vanilla `Building` with
  two ThingDef fields doing the entire block, both re-confirmed this pass
  against the live 1.6 decompile:

    - `passability Impassable` — Verse.AI/PathGrid.cs:140-148's per-Thing
      cost loop reads `thing.def.passability`/`thing.def.pathCost` for ANY
      spawned Thing on a cell, not just the Fire-specific perceivedStatic
      branch further down (:179-204, the one the spike pass already found
      only matches runtime type RimWorld.Fire). This makes the cell a flat
      10000 (ImpassableCost) for literally any pawn's path search — a
      genuinely IMPASSABLE wall, stronger than what real Fire gets (Fire
      only adds +1000 own-cell / +150 adjacent, an avoid-if-possible
      preference, not a hard block) — which matches the sheet's own "a wall
      of flame and smoke nothing crosses" framing better than subclassing
      Fire would have.
    - `pathfinderDangerous true` — a SECOND, independent, fully generic
      ThingDef flag (Verse/ThingDef.cs:175) this pass found beyond what the
      spike pass's own finding named: consumed by
      Verse/PersistentDangerSource.cs and Verse/PathFinderMapData.cs:111 to
      mark the cell in a separate "persistent danger" grid the smarter
      long-range pathfinder search avoids before it even reaches local step
      costing. Vanilla Fire itself does NOT set this flag (confirmed —
      Fire's own def carries no pathfinderDangerous), so this is additional
      avoidance strength real fire doesn't have.

  Why not subclass Fire instead: Fire's own Tick/TickInterval carries a lot
  of behavior this content does not want inheriting unmodified — random
  spread to unrelated cells (TrySpread), pawn ignition on proximity,
  rain/vacuum extinguishing, and its own independent 7500-tick auto-burn-
  floor timer that would race against this def's own INVENTED 12-24h
  lifecycle. A plain Building with two XML fields is simpler, fully
  reviewable, and (per above) gives a STRONGER, more spec-faithful block
  than inheriting Fire would have — a genuine improvement the spike
  pass's own "or carry pathCost/impassable directly" fallback undersold as
  a hedge; it is the better answer, not the fallback one.

  Lifecycle: RM_CompTimedTerrainBurn (new this pass, RM_EnvironmentalHazards
  Source/RM_CompTimedTerrainBurn.cs) — starts the sibling CompReleaseGas on
  spawn (vanilla's own comp never auto-starts), counts down
  durationTicksRange (INVENTED, spec's own "12-24 in-game hours" = 30000-
  60000 ticks), then explicitly calls TerrainGrid.Notify_TerrainBurned on
  its own cell (NOT automatic without a real Fire instance — see that
  class's header) before self-destructing. marksColumnSource true feeds
  RM_MapComponent_ThresholdSmokeColumn (new this pass) for the spec's own
  "distant column... while >= N blaze cells live" cosmetic, INVENTED N=20.

  CompReleaseGas: stock, GasType.BlindSmoke (verified,
  RimWorld/CompReleaseGas.cs / Verse/GasType.cs) — already blocks shooting
  (ShotReport) and AI target LOS (AttackTargetFinder), per the kit spec's
  own citations; no new code needed for that half. cellsToFill/durationSeconds
  are this pass's own INVENTED placeholder tuning (not spec-named beyond
  "blinding smoke").

  Sight/graphic: texPath reuses vanilla Fire's OWN real texPath
  (Things/Special/Fire, Graphic_Flicker, TransparentPostLight shaderType —
  confirmed this pass via mcp__rimsage__get_def_details("Fire")) — a
  deliberate, literal reuse (this thing IS meant to read as fire), not a
  missing-art placeholder; no DEPLOY_HOLD needed.

  Never player-buildable (spawned only by RM_CompFloodIgniter's own
  FireUtility.TryStartFireIn call): no costList, no designationCategory.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_TarBlaze</defName>
    <label>tar blaze</label>
    <description>A cell of poured tar, burning. Blinding smoke pours off it; nothing crosses while it burns.</description>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <category>Building</category>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Special/Fire</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Flicker</graphicClass>
      <shaderType>TransparentPostLight</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <altitudeLayer>PawnState</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <pathfinderDangerous>true</pathfinderDangerous>
    <pathCost>10000</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.3</fillPercent>
    <size>(1,1)</size>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <destroyable>true</destroyable>
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <scatterableOnMapGen>false</scatterableOnMapGen>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimWorld.CompProperties_ReleaseGas">
        <gasType>BlindSmoke</gasType>
        <cellsToFill>9</cellsToFill>
        <durationSeconds>60</durationSeconds>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_TimedTerrainBurn">
        <durationTicksRange>30000~60000</durationTicksRange>
        <autoStartReleaseGas>true</autoStartReleaseGas>
        <convertTerrainOnExpiry>true</convertTerrainOnExpiry>
        <destroyOnExpiry>true</destroyOnExpiry>
        <marksColumnSource>true</marksColumnSource>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
